      "## Put the workflow into service\n\nBefore launch, publish the secure-print release queue failure trigger, required record, permitted frontline actions, stopping conditions, decision owners, customer wording, update interval, after-hours route, evidence retention rule, and closure test in one controlled procedure. Give the ordinary support role a synthetic case and ask a second operator to continue from the handoff without private explanation. Record every missing field, unavailable permission, ambiguous instruction, inaccessible step, and owner-capacity gap. Correct those mechanisms, repeat the exercise with different evidence, and launch only the portion that the buyer can observe, govern, and reverse.",
